---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description="Fullstack developer based in Florianópolis. Building financial systems, AR platforms, and writing about it."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-void text-parchment">
    <Header />

    <main class="relative z-10 min-h-screen pt-28 pb-20 px-8 md:px-14">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

        <!-- Page title -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-16">
          <span class="w-6 h-px bg-signal"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase">About</span>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_280px] gap-16">

          <!-- Bio -->
          <div>
            <h1 class="font-display text-6xl md:text-8xl text-parchment tracking-wide leading-none mb-10">
              EDUARDO<br />DE BEM
            </h1>

            <div class="prose max-w-none">
              <p>
                Fullstack developer based in Florianópolis, SC. Currently at Zallpy building a financial
                platform for BMW USA — Angular Micro Frontends on the front, .NET and MuleSoft behind it,
                all wired through Amazon API Gateway. Alongside that, I've been deep in a separate project
                for the past six months: React + Vite, NestJS, PostgreSQL, and RabbitMQ.
              </p>

              <p>
                Before Zallpy I was at eTopocart working on geoprocessing software — the kind of frontend
                work that involves rendering 10,000-row tables without the browser giving up, and making
                different browser tabs talk to each other. It was a good place to learn that performance
                problems are usually more interesting than they look.
              </p>

              <p>
                In 2023 I spent a year between the US and Europe. Went to sharpen my English. Came back
                with that plus a clearer idea of what I actually want to build.
              </p>

              <p>
                I used to play violin — seriously, for years. I don't anymore. But the same instincts
                carry over: you can tell when something is slightly off even if you can't name it yet,
                and the only way to get good at something is to show up before you're ready.
              </p>

              <p>
                I'm studying Computer Science at UNISUL (graduating 2026) and volunteer on a WebGL-based
                augmented reality project there — which is how I ended up comfortable enough with 3D
                rendering to put a Three.js terrain on this homepage.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-4xl mt-12 mb-4">WHAT I WORK WITH</h2>
              <p>
                On the frontend: TypeScript, React, Angular, and Micro Frontend architectures day-to-day.
                On the backend: Node.js, NestJS, and .NET depending on the project. I've worked with
                PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, MuleSoft, and AWS (API Gateway, Lambda). I pick up what the problem
                needs — the stack debate is usually less interesting than the problem itself.
              </p>

              <h2 class="text-4xl mt-12 mb-4">GET IN TOUCH</h2>
              <p>
                If you want to talk about a project, a role, or just found something here worth discussing —
                <a href="mailto:eduardogdebem@gmail.com" class="text-signal hover:text-parchment transition-colors">
                  send me an email
                </a>
                or find me on
                <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/eduardogdebem" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-signal hover:text-parchment transition-colors">
                  LinkedIn
                </a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Sidebar -->
          <aside class="lg:pt-2">
            <div class="border-l border-trench pl-8 space-y-10">

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Currently</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['Zallpy — Fullstack Pleno', 'BMW financial platform', 'React/NestJS/RabbitMQ project'].map(item => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-signal rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {item}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Reading</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['Sci-fi', 'Fantasy', 'Whatever catches me'].map(tag => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-signal rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {tag}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Racing</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['Formula 1', 'Constructor standings > driver standings'].map(tag => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-signal rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {tag}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Fighting</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['MMA', 'Boxing', 'Combat sports in general'].map(tag => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-signal rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {tag}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Music</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['Ex-violinist', 'Still listens'].map(tag => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-field rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {tag}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="font-mono text-xs text-brush tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Languages</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2">
                  {['Portuguese — native', 'English — advanced', 'Spanish — intermediate'].map(tag => (
                    <li class="font-sans text-sm text-parchment flex items-center gap-2">
                      <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-brush rounded-full shrink-0"></span>
                      {tag}
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>

            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
